# About 30 Sources

Your evidence, kept as it arrived: documents, web captures, meeting and interview records, and context you simply spoke aloud. Every source is dated and attributed, and it stays the way it was captured — later understanding is added around it, never written over it, so the trail back to what you were actually handed stays intact. Notes in `20 Knowledge/` cite the sources they rest on. Binary files — photographs, audio, and the untouched originals of documents that were converted to text — sit in `Attachments/`.
